le":"Isolate tool execution","verification":"In a test environment, attempt reads outside the workspace, forbidden network connections, and resource exhaustion; retain policy and denial evidence."}],"finding_ids":["b1b0f0a3f33fe93875fcb58a"],"id":"group-45290f4fa5c7","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Trace the input to eval/exec and replace it with fixed operations; if generated execution is essential, isolate it before accepting untrusted input.","locations":[{"end_line":16,"finding_id":"b1b0f0a3f33fe93875fcb58a","line":16,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If external or generated content reaches this expression, it could execute Python with the process identity and access its files, credentials, and network.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI001","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-TOOLS","OWASP-AGENT-CS","OWASP-LLM2026","TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"},{"id":"OWASP-LLM2026","title":"OWASP GenAI LLM Top 10 2026","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-genai-llm-top-10-2026/"},{"id":"TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY","title":"Python Security Considerations","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/security_warnings.html"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Agent/tool developer","title":"Dynamic Python code execution"},{"confidence_counts":{"medium":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["EXEC-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["AGT-01","AUTH-02","MCP-02"],"how_it_helps":"Have an execution service allow only named operations, permitted argument values, and caller-owned target resources before invoking a tool.","id":"tool-policy","residual_limit":"Authorized operations can still be harmful when business constraints are incomplete; prompt instructions cannot enforce this boundary.","source_ids":["OWASP-AGENT-CS","MCP-TOOLS"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Enforce action policy outside the model","verification":"Exercise disallowed operations, additional arguments, cross-tenant identifiers, and direct calls that bypass the agent planner."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-02","SUP-05","OPS-02"],"how_it_helps":"Run the risky tool in a separate, disposable identity with no host mounts, ambient credentials, or unnecessary outbound access.","id":"execution-isolation","residual_limit":"Isolation limits reachable assets; it does not make injected code trustworthy or rule out a runtime escape.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Isolate tool execution","verification":"In a test environment, attempt reads outside the workspace, forbidden network connections, and resource exhaustion; retain policy and denial evidence."}],"finding_ids":["0fa7e450cd583d78646ef397"],"id":"group-f0e53150bfd5","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Replace os.system/os.popen with a fixed executable and validated argument list; trace all contributing values.","locations":[{"end_line":10,"finding_id":"0fa7e450cd583d78646ef397","line":10,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If external values contribute to the command string, the shell could execute additional commands with the server identity.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI003","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-TOOLS","OWASP-AGENT-CS","OWASP-LLM2026","OWASP-MCP10","OWASP-OUTPUT2025","TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"},{"id":"OWASP-LLM2026","title":"OWASP GenAI LLM Top 10 2026","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-genai-llm-top-10-2026/"},{"id":"OWASP-MCP10","title":"OWASP MCP Top 10","url":"https://owasp.org/projects/mcp-top-10"},{"id":"OWASP-OUTPUT2025","title":"LLM05:2025 Improper Output Handling","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm052025-improper-output-handling/"},{"id":"TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY","title":"Python Security Considerations","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/security_warnings.html"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Agent/tool developer","title":"Dynamic os shell command"},{"confidence_counts":{"medium":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["EXEC-06"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["SUP-03","DATA-04"],"how_it_helps":"Require reviewed artifact provenance plus a digest or signature checked against an independently trusted identity or manifest.","id":"artifact-verification","residual_limit":"Authenticity establishes the producer and bytes; an approved producer can still ship vulnerable or malicious content.","source_ids":["SLSA-12","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING"],"sources":[{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Verify artifact identity before use","verification":"Substitute bytes, producer identity, or verification metadata in a controlled test and confirm the consumer rejects the artifact."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-06","SUP-06"],"how_it_helps":"Perform necessary conversion of legacy serialized artifacts in a disposable environment without production data or credentials.","id":"isolated-conversion","residual_limit":"Conversion output still needs integrity, format, and downstream behavior review; isolation is not proof of benign content.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","TECH-PYTORCH-SERIAL"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"TECH-PYTORCH-SERIAL","title":"PyTorch Serialization semantics","url":"https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/notes/serialization.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Separate artifact conversion from production","verification":"Demonstrate that a conversion job cannot reach production services and only approved output formats are promoted."}],"finding_ids":["d2d09fb2875db72f18779bfc"],"id":"group-9ee5075ce1a1","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Establish who can produce and replace the input; migrate to a nonexecutable data format or restrict verified legacy artifacts to an isolated conversion path.","locations":[{"end_line":12,"finding_id":"d2d09fb2875db72f18779bfc","line":12,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If an attacker can supply or replace the serialized input, loading it may execute code even before the application examines the returned object.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI005","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","NIST-SSDF","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","SLSA-12","TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY","TECH-PYTORCH-SERIAL"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"},{"id":"TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY","title":"Python Security Considerations","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/security_warnings.html"},{"id":"TECH-PYTORCH-SERIAL","title":"PyTorch Serialization semantics","url":"https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/notes/serialization.html"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Application/model pipeline owner","title":"Executable deserialization requires trusted inputs"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["MCP-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["MCP-01","AUTH-05"],"how_it_helps":"Use verified TLS on every relevant network hop, with an appropriate public or private CA and validated service hostname.","id":"trusted-transport","residual_limit":"TLS does not protect data from an authorized endpoint, compromised gateway, or plaintext segments beyond termination.","source_ids":["MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Require authenticated encrypted transport","verification":"Present an untrusted, expired, or wrong-host certificate and verify rejection; inspect backend traffic after TLS termination."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-05","AGT-07","SUP-05"],"how_it_helps":"Enforce an outbound policy outside the application that permits only required destinations and services; include IPv6 and proxy paths.","id":"egress-policy","residual_limit":"Allowed destinations may themselves accept leaked data; destination rules do not replace content and action authorization.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Restrict outbound destinations independently","verification":"From the deployed identity, test direct IP, DNS, redirect, metadata-service, and proxy-mediated attempts to prohibited destinations."}],"finding_ids":["07fc5f6fd7699fd0194dc479"],"id":"group-08a6f7f32c94","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Enable certificate and hostname verification; install the intended CA for a private gateway and test rejection of an untrusted certificate.","locations":[{"end_line":11,"finding_id":"07fc5f6fd7699fd0194dc479","line":11,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If a network intermediary can impersonate the destination, disabled verification may expose or alter credentials, prompts, and tool responses.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI006","severity":"high","source_ids":["CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC","MCP-HTTP","MCP-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"},{"id":"MCP-HTTP","title":"MCP: Streamable HTTP transport","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/streamable-http"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Application and gateway owner","title":"TLS certificate verification disabled"},{"confidence_counts":{"medium":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["AUTH-05","DATA-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","OPS-06"],"how_it_helps":"For a real exposed credential, identify reachable systems, revoke or rotate it, and review access records for misuse.","id":"exposure-response","residual_limit":"Successful rotation stops future use of that credential but cannot reverse access or data loss that already occurred.","source_ids":["CISA-JCDC","NIST-SSDF"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-JCDC","title":"JCDC AI Cybersecurity Collaboration Playbook and Fact Sheet (release notice)","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2025/01/14/cisa-releases-jcdc-ai-cybersecurity-collaboration-playbook-and-fact-sheet"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Investigate and contain confirmed secret exposure","verification":"Confirm the old credential no longer works and record the exposure window, affected copies, and follow-up owner."},{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","DATA-01","DATA-06"],"how_it_helps":"Load secrets at runtime through an approved store or workload identity; keep them out of source, artifacts, and model context.","id":"credential-lifecycle","residual_limit":"Deleting a file or hiding a later image layer does not revoke a credential or erase copies already distributed.","source_ids":["MCP-AUTH","JOINT-AGENTIC"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Use managed credential injection and revocation","verification":"Test rotation and revocation without disclosing values; inspect build layers and launch metadata for retained copies."},{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","AUTH-09"],"how_it_helps":"Give this component a distinct identity and only the downstream scopes and lifetime needed for its approved operations.","id":"secret-boundary","residual_limit":"A compromised component can still use its allowed permissions until credentials expire or revocation takes effect.","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Limit credentials available to the workload","verification":"Use its runtime identity to attempt forbidden service operations, then revoke it and confirm subsequent access fails."}],"finding_ids":["afb2bdb94696690028650faf"],"id":"group-57a1992f928c","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Determine whether the value is real without reproducing it; revoke or rotate a real exposed credential and remove retained copies through the incident process.","locations":[{"end_line":6,"finding_id":"afb2bdb94696690028650faf","line":6,"path":"mcp.json"}],"plausible_impact":"If the detected literal is a live credential, anyone with access to the source, image layers, or copied artifacts may use its granted permissions.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI010","severity":"high","source_ids":["CISA-JCDC","CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","JOINT-AGENTIC","JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC","MCP-SECURITY","NIST-SSDF"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-JCDC","title":"JCDC AI Cybersecurity Collaboration Playbook and Fact Sheet (release notice)","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2025/01/14/cisa-releases-jcdc-ai-cybersecurity-collaboration-playbook-and-fact-sheet"},{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Credential/service owner","title":"Credential-like literal in source or configuration"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["MCP-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["MCP-01","AUTH-05"],"how_it_helps":"Use verified TLS on every relevant network hop, with an appropriate public or private CA and validated service hostname.","id":"trusted-transport","residual_limit":"TLS does not protect data from an authorized endpoint, compromised gateway, or plaintext segments beyond termination.","source_ids":["MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Require authenticated encrypted transport","verification":"Present an untrusted, expired, or wrong-host certificate and verify rejection; inspect backend traffic after TLS termination."},{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","AUTH-09"],"how_it_helps":"Give this component a distinct identity and only the downstream scopes and lifetime needed for its approved operations.","id":"secret-boundary","residual_limit":"A compromised component can still use its allowed permissions until credentials expire or revocation takes effect.","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Limit credentials available to the workload","verification":"Use its runtime identity to attempt forbidden service operations, then revoke it and confirm subsequent access fails."}],"finding_ids":["d841174f55e032505f8136b9"],"id":"group-b69c379f05c4","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Use HTTPS with verified certificates; if a separate protected transport is intentional, document and test every network hop and termination boundary.","locations":[{"end_line":10,"finding_id":"d841174f55e032505f8136b9","line":10,"path":"mcp.json"}],"plausible_impact":"If remote traffic traverses an unprotected link, observers or intermediaries may read or modify MCP credentials, requests, and responses.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI029","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC","MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC","MCP-HTTP","MCP-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"},{"id":"MCP-HTTP","title":"MCP: Streamable HTTP transport","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/streamable-http"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"MCP/gateway owner","title":"Remote MCP URL uses plaintext HTTP"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["AGT-01","AGT-02","MCP-09","SUP-05"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["AGT-01","AUTH-02","MCP-02"],"how_it_helps":"Have an execution service allow only named operations, permitted argument values, and caller-owned target resources before invoking a tool.","id":"tool-policy","residual_limit":"Authorized operations can still be harmful when business constraints are incomplete; prompt instructions cannot enforce this boundary.","source_ids":["OWASP-AGENT-CS","MCP-TOOLS"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Enforce action policy outside the model","verification":"Exercise disallowed operations, additional arguments, cross-tenant identifiers, and direct calls that bypass the agent planner."},{"control_ids":["AGT-02","OPS-04"],"how_it_helps":"Require an independent approval for the exact actor, tool, normalized arguments, target, and expiry before irreversible effects occur.","id":"action-approval","residual_limit":"Approval cannot compensate for misleading previews, excessive approver authority, or actions that happen before the check.","source_ids":["OWASP-AGENT-CS"],"sources":[{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Bind sensitive actions to explicit approval","verification":"Change arguments after approval, replay the approval, and call after expiry; each attempt must be denied before a side effect."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-02","SUP-05","OPS-02"],"how_it_helps":"Run the risky tool in a separate, disposable identity with no host mounts, ambient credentials, or unnecessary outbound access.","id":"execution-isolation","residual_limit":"Isolation limits reachable assets; it does not make injected code trustworthy or rule out a runtime escape.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Isolate tool execution","verification":"In a test environment, attempt reads outside the workspace, forbidden network connections, and resource exhaustion; retain policy and denial evidence."}],"finding_ids":["592fbfc9b7dab062dc97906c"],"id":"group-0a77dbbc61c4","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Review the effective permission policy and restore bounded tools and runtime isolation; require independent approval for the specific sensitive effects.","locations":[{"end_line":7,"finding_id":"592fbfc9b7dab062dc97906c","line":7,"path":"mcp.json"}],"plausible_impact":"If unrestricted execution or disabled approval is effective, malicious context or an erroneous plan may reach sensitive actions with the agent identity.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI031","severity":"high","source_ids":["ASD-HARNESS","JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-SECURITY","MCP-TOOLS","OWASP-AGENT-CS","OWASP-LLM2026","OWASP-MCP-CS"],"sources":[{"id":"ASD-HARNESS","title":"Agentic AI harnesses: The layer above the model","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/agentic-ai-harnesses"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"},{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"},{"id":"OWASP-LLM2026","title":"OWASP GenAI LLM Top 10 2026","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-genai-llm-top-10-2026/"},{"id":"OWASP-MCP-CS","title":"MCP Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Agent/platform owner","title":"Agent approval or sandbox safeguard explicitly bypassed"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["MCP-09","SUP-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["SUP-01","SUP-03"],"how_it_helps":"Use a committed lock or approved artifact manifest, enforce it during installation, and retain the resolved dependency inventory.","id":"immutable-install","residual_limit":"An exact version or digest can still identify a vulnerable artifact; mutable transitive dependencies must also be constrained.","source_ids":["NIST-SSDF","OPENSSF-BASELINE-202608"],"sources":[{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"OPENSSF-BASELINE-202608","title":"Open Source Project Security Baseline","url":"https://baseline.openssf.org/versions/2026-08-28"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Resolve and install reviewed dependency bytes","verification":"Build in a clean environment and compare resolved bytes; modify a lock or artifact and verify the release gate rejects it."},{"control_ids":["SUP-03","DATA-04"],"how_it_helps":"Require reviewed artifact provenance plus a digest or signature checked against an independently trusted identity or manifest.","id":"artifact-verification","residual_limit":"Authenticity establishes the producer and bytes; an approved producer can still ship vulnerable or malicious content.","source_ids":["SLSA-12","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING"],"sources":[{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Verify artifact identity before use","verification":"Substitute bytes, producer identity, or verification metadata in a controlled test and confirm the consumer rejects the artifact."},{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","AUTH-09"],"how_it_helps":"Give this component a distinct identity and only the downstream scopes and lifetime needed for its approved operations.","id":"secret-boundary","residual_limit":"A compromised component can still use its allowed permissions until credentials expire or revocation takes effect.","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Limit credentials available to the workload","verification":"Use its runtime identity to attempt forbidden service operations, then revoke it and confirm subsequent access fails."}],"finding_ids":["6b77081a826c4c6833edc47f"],"id":"group-964934e5a62a","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Resolve and approve exact executable and transitive artifacts, enforce the lock at launch, and minimize inherited environment secrets.","locations":[{"end_line":4,"finding_id":"6b77081a826c4c6833edc47f","line":4,"path":"mcp.json"}],"plausible_impact":"If the package runner resolves a changed or malicious artifact, the next MCP launch could execute different code with the client environment permissions.","priority":"P2","rule_id":"AI018","severity":"medium","source_ids":["CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","JOINT-AGENTIC","MCP-SECURITY","NIST-SSDF","OPENSSF-BASELINE-202608","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","OWASP-MCP-CS","SLSA-12"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"OPENSSF-BASELINE-202608","title":"Open Source Project Security Baseline","url":"https://baseline.openssf.org/versions/2026-08-28"},{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"OWASP-MCP-CS","title":"MCP Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"MCP integration/build owner","title":"MCP package runner resolves an unpinned artifact"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["SUP-05"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["SUP-05","TEST-05"],"how_it_helps":"Use a dedicated nonroot identity, minimal capabilities, no privilege escalation, and an enforced syscall and mandatory-access policy where supported.","id":"runtime-restrictions","residual_limit":"Nonroot alone is insufficient; writable mounts, added capabilities, host namespaces, and kernel flaws can weaken isolation.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","CIS-CONTROLS-81"],"sources":[{"id":"CIS-CONTROLS-81","title":"CIS Critical Security Controls v8.1","url":"https://www.cisecurity.org/controls/v8-1"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Apply runtime isolation controls together","verification":"Inspect the effective workload and attempt privileged operations, prohibited syscalls, and access to protected host resources."},{"control_ids":["SUP-05","TEST-04","GOV-02"],"how_it_helps":"Place tools needing exceptional privileges in a separate environment with narrow interfaces and no unrelated tenant data.","id":"workload-separation","residual_limit":"Shared kernels or administrative infrastructure may retain common failure paths; a container is not automatically a strong hostile-code boundary.","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC","CSA-CCM"],"sources":[{"id":"CSA-CCM","title":"Cloud Controls Matrix and CAIQ v4.1","url":"https://cloudsecurityalliance.org/artifacts/cloud-controls-matrix-v4-1"},{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Separate risky tools from sensitive workloads","verification":"Test cross-workload network and filesystem access and confirm the privileged component cannot impersonate the requesting agent."}],"finding_ids":["20771a324af20de316ec34f9"],"id":"group-f42ebc88841c","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Verify the final build stage and deployed user, then run with a dedicated nonroot identity unless a documented operation requires otherwise.","locations":[{"end_line":3,"finding_id":"20771a324af20de316ec34f9","line":2,"path":"Dockerfile"}],"plausible_impact":"If this is the effective runtime user, a tool compromise may gain more authority within the container; host impact depends on mounts, capabilities, user mappings, and kernel isolation.","priority":"P2","rule_id":"AI021","severity":"medium","source_ids":["CIS-CONTROLS-81","CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","CSA-CCM","JOINT-AGENTIC","JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":[{"id":"CIS-CONTROLS-81","title":"CIS Critical Security Controls v8.1","url":"https://www.cisecurity.org/controls/v8-1"},{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"CSA-CCM","title":"Cloud Controls Matrix and CAIQ v4.1","url":"https://cloudsecurityalliance.org/artifacts/cloud-controls-matrix-v4-1"},{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Container/platform owner","title":"Container explicitly runs as root"},{"confidence_counts":{"low":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["SUP-01","SUP-03"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["SUP-03","DATA-04"],"how_it_helps":"Require reviewed artifact provenance plus a digest or signature checked against an independently trusted identity or manifest.","id":"artifact-verification","residual_limit":"Authenticity establishes the producer and bytes; an approved producer can still ship vulnerable or malicious content.","source_ids":["SLSA-12","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING"],"sources":[{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Verify artifact identity before use","verification":"Substitute bytes, producer identity, or verification metadata in a controlled test and confirm the consumer rejects the artifact."},{"control_ids":["SUP-02","SUP-04","OPS-05"],"how_it_helps":"Review known-vulnerability and maintenance evidence for the actual resolved artifacts and apply updates through a repeatable release process.","id":"maintenance-loop","residual_limit":"This source/image scan does not provide a current CVE verdict, and a vulnerability database cannot identify every unknown flaw.","source_ids":["NIST-SSDF","OPENSSF-SCORECARD"],"sources":[{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"OPENSSF-SCORECARD","title":"OpenSSF Scorecard","url":"https://securityscorecards.dev/"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Keep pinned artifacts maintained","verification":"Demonstrate a dependency update, relevant regression checks, and deployment or rollback of the resulting approved artifact."}],"finding_ids":["055ed29e5f56926f1827a0b8"],"id":"group-0cc3d39352a0","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Identify the approved image digest and enforce it in the effective build or deployment while preserving a reviewed update process.","locations":[{"end_line":1,"finding_id":"055ed29e5f56926f1827a0b8","line":1,"path":"Dockerfile"}],"plausible_impact":"If a mutable image tag changes, a rebuild or deployment may consume unreviewed bytes; the scan does not establish that the current image is vulnerable.","priority":"P3","rule_id":"AI024","severity":"low","source_ids":["CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","NIST-SSDF","NSA-DATA","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","OPENSSF-SCORECARD","SLSA-12"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"NSA-DATA","title":"AI Data Security: Best Practices for Securing Data Used to Train & Operate AI Systems (NSA announcement)","url":"https://www.nsa.gov/Press-Room/Press-Releases-Statements/Press-Release-View/Article/4192332/nsas-aisc-releases-joint-guidance-on-the-risks-and-best-practices-in-ai-data-se/"},{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"OPENSSF-SCORECARD","title":"OpenSSF Scorec